        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: задержка",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "задержка (zadérzhka) — \"a delay\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Из-за тумана была большая задержка. Iz-za tumána bylá bolsháya zadérzhka. Because of the fog there was a long delay."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Рейс с задержкой — a delayed flight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "задержка (zadérzhka) is built on задержать 'to hold back', from за- and держать 'to hold'. Держать is inherited from Proto-Slavic dĭržati 'to hold' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
